@startuml qnx_dispatch_engine_client_pulses_activity
title QnxDispatchEngine - client pulse dispatch

start
:Client worker dispatches SelectPulseCallback\nor CoidDeathPulseCallback;
if (Entry is SelectPulseCallback?) then (yes)
    :Unpack the pulse pointer value into index, signal and nonce;
    if (Index out of range, nonce mismatch,\nor slot endpoint is nullptr?) then (drop)
        :Return 0 without invoking an endpoint callback;
        stop
    else (valid slot)
        :Inspect the decoded signal;
    endif
    if (Signal equals kSignalPing?) then (yes)
        :Invoke endpoint.ping();
    else (other)
        :Invoke endpoint.input();
    endif
    :Return 0;
    stop
else (CoidDeathPulseCallback)
    :Read the coid from the pulse integer value;
endif

:ConnectServerInfo(0, coid, nullptr);
if (Lookup succeeds and returns the same coid?) then (yes)
    :Log an obsolete death pulse and return 0;
    stop
else (error or different coid)
    :Find a non-null poll endpoint with fd equal to coid;
endif
if (An endpoint is found?) then (yes)
    :Log the crash-pulse path;
    :Invoke endpoint.input();
else (not found)
    :Skip endpoint delivery;
endif
:Return 0;
stop

legend
    All actions here execute on the client runner's worker.
    Only new-data and ping values are constructed during local registration.
    SelectPulseCallback sends every non-ping signal on its input branch.
    A death pulse triggers input, not a direct disconnect or descriptor close.
    Receive-error and connection-lifecycle handling belong to the consumer.
endlegend

@enduml
